hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19101","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from Husayn ibn al-Harith al-Jadali, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab addressed on the day about which there is doubt, and he said: Lo, I have sat with the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked them; lo, they told me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast on seeing it and break the fast on seeing it, and if you doubt it, then if it is obscured from you complete thirty, and if two Muslim witnesses testify then fast and break the fast."
